The '''Five Veils Route'''<ref name="Bespin">{{EncyclopediaCite|Bespin and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> was a [[hyperspace route]] that branched off<ref name="Map" /> the [[Triellus Trade Route]]<ref name="Triellus" /> at the [[Farstine system]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]] and headed south through [[Sterdic IV]], [[Vallt]], [[Pastoria]], [[Yar Togna]], [[Idaflor]],<ref name="Map" /> [[Quence]],<ref name="AVG" /> the [[Chagar system]] and ended at the [[Svivren system]].<ref name="Map" /> A second branch of the route began at [[Quence]],<ref name="AVG" /> ran eastward to [[Nixus]], [[Guat'a]],<ref name="Map" /> [[Gallimere]], and ended at the [[Skynara system]].<ref name="AVG" />

{{Route-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, this hyperlane was known as the [[Five Veils Route]] and was first mapped in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]''.<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref> The route originated as the Five Veils' Tour trade route in ''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]'', which established it as running from Farstine to Skynara,<ref name="GG9">''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]''</ref> but ''The Essential Atlas'' added another branch south to Svivren,<ref name="TEA" /> and the book's author [[Jason Fry]] stated that the two routes were the same but used for tourism versus shipping.<ref name="Fry">{{JCFCite|url=posts/50723299|board=Literature|thread=The Essential Atlas and Galactic Cartography: Official Discussion|user=[[Jason Fry|jasonfry]]|date=2013-05-16}}</ref>

